       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum daily dose, and it could seriously harm the patient. You've also said you aren't a clinician, so you aren't the person who should be confirming a dose like this. I'd need that confirmation from the prescriber.\n\nWhat I can do:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the standard range.** A prescriber can specify 2.5, 5, or 10 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Pass along a prescriber's confirmation.** If a licensed prescriber has a real clinical reason for 50 mg, they should enter or co-sign the order themselves and talk to pharmacy. I'd also want a note documenting the rationale.\n\nIf you tell me who the prescriber is, or give me a corrected dose, I'll continue from there."
